  "title": "Total boundedness in L²(B̆_1) of Lipschitz sequences with bounded W^{1,2} energy",
  "statement": "Let n ∈ ℕ, M ∈ ℝ and (u_j)_{j∈ℕ} be Lipschitz functions ℝⁿ → ℝ (ℝⁿ = Euclid n, each with its own constant) such that ∫_B u_j² ≤ M and ∫_B ‖Du_j‖² ≤ M for every j, where B := B̆_1(0) and Du_j = fderiv ℝ u_j. Then for every η > 0 there is a finite set S ⊆ ℕ such that every j has some k ∈ S with ∫_B (u_j − u_k)² ≤ η.",
